                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The gameplay kinda sucks. I mean it's fine if you're into this kind of game.\nYou're in a lab maze where you gotta find your way to the exit.\nThe thing is you gotta die many times to even explore each maze as it drops extra time where you die.\nJust need 1 person to find and make a guide with all the exit and you're done. \nThere's two interesting powerups you can pickup which are the speedup and the timefreeze which are useful.\nThe game tracks your time when you finish a level.\nI guess the game would be better if it had also leaderboard and checkpoints you could explore to make it easier(or just remove the timelimit nonsense).\nBut the game is Unity based and suffers from random freezes/laggyness when cruising the spaceship like halls. Completely unacceptable for a simple game like this one should be.\nFortunately there's only 15 levels to play through, so it's not all that bad.\n\nI'd say better skip this and go with SEUM: Speedrunners from Hell. It's a much better game than this anyway.\n\n\nEdit: Found all of the 15 labirinth exits somehow and finished the game in 2 hours with some setbacks xD",
